Slayer 1.0: MainWindow::RemoveProcessItems() deletes the thread rows of the
remove list in its first loop, but leaves their pointers in the list; the
second loop then dynamic_casts every entry, the deleted ones too, which
reads their vtable pointers from freed memory. That worked while freed
blocks kept their bytes. Prose's allocator of patch 0138 wrote into freed
blocks, and Slayer crashed at the first refresh after a thread ended
(0140 made the allocator leave freed blocks alone again, which hides the
bug but does not fix it). Clear the entry once its row is deleted.

--- a/src/MainWindow.cpp
+++ b/src/MainWindow.cpp
@@ -404,6 +404,8 @@
 				team_item->thread_items_list->del(p1->thread);
 
 			delete p1;
+			// the loop below must not dynamic_cast the deleted item
+			items->ReplaceItem(i, NULL);
 		}
 	}
 
